WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:15.820
slammed the album shut.

2
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.560
“Did you see that?”

3
00:00:19.041 --> 00:00:20.881
he asked, his voice shaking.

4
00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:23.622
“That pyramid was glowing!”

5
00:00:24.362 --> 00:00:25.722
Mandy nodded slowly.

6
00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:29.223
“Should we tell Mom and Dad?”

7
00:00:30.524 --> 00:00:31.604
Vinnie shook his head.

8
00:00:32.368 --> 00:00:34.589
“No, this is our little secret.”

9
00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:40.311
“There was something written below the picture,” Mandy said.

10
00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:42.412
“Maybe we should read it.”

11
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:45.994
Vinnie nodded and opened the album.

12
00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:49.075
The handwriting was small and neat.

13
00:00:49.095 --> 00:00:56.798
“‘August 24, my first photo travels,’” Mandy read aloud.

14
00:00:56.818 --> 00:00:59.299
“Photo travels?

15
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.500
What’s that?”

16
00:01:01.156 --> 00:01:02.156
Vinnie interrupted.

17
00:01:03.337 --> 00:01:04.897
Mandy continued to read.

18
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:09.118
“‘I found this photo album in my uncle’s attic.

19
00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:12.839
It didn’t look special on the outside.

20
00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:18.021
But once I opened it, it changed my life forever.’”

21
00:01:18.041 --> 00:01:23.162
“So he found the album in an attic too,” said Vinnie.

22
00:01:24.242 --> 00:01:26.403
Nodding, Mandy continued to read.

23
00:01:26.423 --> 00:01:29.384
“‘People say I’m crazy.

24
00:01:30.044 --> 00:01:31.044
Maybe I am.

25
00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:34.625
But I have traveled to the past.

26
00:01:35.986 --> 00:01:39.146
I even have proof—this photo album.’”

27
00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:41.807
“Travel to the past?

28
00:01:42.247 --> 00:01:43.708
Like in a time machine?”

29
00:01:44.748 --> 00:01:46.168
Vinnie asked excitedly.

30
00:01:46.188 --> 00:01:47.489
“Go on reading!”

31
00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:55.911
“'My first Egypt Mandy held her breath.

32
00:01:55.931 --> 00:01:59.612
“'A glowing pyramid called to me.'”

33
00:02:00.916 --> 00:02:04.359
“Mandy, do you think it’s calling to us too?”

34
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.000
Vinnie asked.

35
00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:09.083
He pulled the photo out of the album.

36
00:02:10.023 --> 00:02:15.308
Mandy continued, “‘When I looked into the light, my adventures began.’”

37
00:02:15.328 --> 00:02:18.670
"But how did he go back in time?

38
00:02:19.231 --> 00:02:20.992
And why do the pictures glow?”

39
00:02:22.413 --> 00:02:23.995
Vinnie stared at the photo.

40
00:02:24.015 --> 00:02:28.058
“Vinnie, maybe we should forget all this.”

41
00:02:28.859 --> 00:02:30.280
Mandy looked at her watch.

42
00:02:31.664 --> 00:02:32.785
It was almost noon.

43
00:02:32.805 --> 00:02:35.987
“Let’s just go and have lunch.”

44
00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:38.469
But Vinnie did not hear her.

45
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.551
His eyes were fixed on the photograph.

46
00:02:41.571 --> 00:02:44.953
“Vinnie, you’re scaring me!

47
00:02:45.113 --> 00:02:46.074
Stop it!”

48
00:02:46.514 --> 00:02:47.095
she cried.

49
00:02:47.115 --> 00:02:49.857
“But what if it’s real?

50
00:02:50.677 --> 00:02:53.499
What if we really could go back in time?”

51
00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.021
Vinnie said in a dreamy voice.

52
00:02:56.041 --> 00:03:00.124
“I’m going downstairs,” Mandy insisted.

53
00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:02.841
Vinnie grabbed her arm.

54
00:03:04.082 --> 00:03:06.283
“Don’t you want an adventure, Mandy?”

55
00:03:06.803 --> 00:03:07.944
he said excitedly.

56
00:03:07.964 --> 00:03:13.147
“I do, but I’m also scared,” she said honestly.

57
00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.928
“How do we travel to the past?

58
00:03:17.289 --> 00:03:20.371
And I’m worried about how we’d get back home again.”

59
00:03:20.391 --> 00:03:24.373
“Mandy,” her brother suddenly shouted.

60
00:03:24.393 --> 00:03:26.935
“The pyramid is getting brighter!”

61
00:03:26.955 --> 00:03:32.606
Sure enough, the pyramid was glowing with a bright yellow light.

62
00:03:34.007 --> 00:03:37.469
Now the children really couldn’t take their eyes off the light.

63
00:03:37.489 --> 00:03:42.151
“‘When I looked into the light, my adventures began.’”

64
00:03:43.352 --> 00:03:46.014
Vinnie repeated the words written in the album.

65
00:03:47.474 --> 00:03:50.416
The heat from the light felt hot against their faces.

66
00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.258
It forced them to close their eyes.

67
00:03:54.538 --> 00:03:56.940
Now they could see the pyramid in their minds.

68
00:03:57.936 --> 00:03:59.617
It seemed to be coming closer.

69
00:03:59.637 --> 00:04:04.580
“Vinnie, I’m scared,” cried Mandy.

70
00:04:06.061 --> 00:04:09.743
Suddenly, the children felt their feet lift off the ground.

71
00:04:10.703 --> 00:04:14.906
Vinnie grabbed his sister’s hand and shouted, “Hang on, Mandy!”

72
00:04:16.066 --> 00:04:17.587
He held her hand tightly.

73
00:04:17.607 --> 00:04:20.128
“I’ve changed my mind!

74
00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:21.729
I don’t want to do this!”

75
00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.010
Vinnie cried.

76
00:04:23.831 --> 00:04:26.132
He tried to open his eyes, but couldn’t.

77
00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.581
It was too bright.

78
00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.663
“Mandy!” “Vinnie!”

79
00:04:32.943 --> 00:04:36.145
Still holding on to each other, the children screamed.

80
00:04:37.106 --> 00:04:40.408
They began to fall down a deep dark tunnel.
